t columns and responsive overrides or logos stack in one column.","layout.responsiveProps":"Responsive xl/l/m/s/xs props exist only on Flex, Row, Column and Grid; Text and Heading take just s={{ hide: true }}. Button and the rest have none: to change one at a breakpoint, wrap it in a Row or Column and put the breakpoint prop there. Text and Heading take padding and flex but no radius or border; put those on the wrapper.","size.rem":"A number on any size, spacing or offset prop is on the token scale in 3.0 (it was rem in 2.x): width={32} renders as width=\"32\" (2rem, 32 px at the defaults, scaled by data-scaling), maxWidth={40} is 2.5rem. For 40rem write the string, maxWidth=\"40rem\". An icon or avatar box is usually \"24\" to \"48\", or 24 to 48 as numbers.","spacing.tokens":"gap, padding and margin take spacing tokens (\"0\", \"1\", \"2\", \"4\", \"8\", \"12\", \"16\", \"20\", \"24\", \"32\", \"40\", \"48\", \"56\", \"64\", \"72\", \"80\", \"104\", \"128\", \"160\", or xs–xl). \"6\" and \"10\" are not tokens and are type errors.","layout.noSpanOrType":"Row, Column and Grid have no span and no type prop. A clickable row is a Button (or a native <button>), and a Grid child spanning columns uses style={{ gridColumn: \"span 2\" }}.","RevealFx.primaryContent":"Never wrap primary content (headlines, prices, KPIs, CTAs) in RevealFx: it stays blurred and unreadable until the reveal ends. Reveal secondary sections only, with duration={1000}.","layout.noBaseline":"vertical and horizontal take start, center, end, between, around, even or stretch. There is no baseline; for baseline-aligned text use style={{ alignItems: \"baseline\" }}.","Chart.xAxis":"The x axis reads the first key of data[0] that is not a series key (date, label, month). Put that key first in every point and list only the plotted keys in series: series={[{ key: \"visitors\" }]} with data={[{ date: \"Oct 1\", visitors: 1840 }]}."},"quality":{"statCard":"Column surface recipe — not Card","kpiNumber":"CountFx 